 https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178629", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e4089a15dd226821192ef0638100bc59b504457b", "parents": ["7a293bbf964ce81228a4ddd5fedd3699713b3150"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan Hunt \u003crhunt@eqrion.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1833339 - wasm: Reserve the right amount of Stk entries. r=yury, a=RyanVM\n\nBaseCompiler::emitCatch will push `tag.params().length() + 1` entries\nto the Stk.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178220", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f5f293bd79791b334f1aefb359231ce051eb73e7", "parents": ["e4089a15dd226821192ef0638100bc59b504457b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1684786147, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "255": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr102 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D179053", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-telemetry-v2.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/onecrl.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5b4d602ef5a54aed21c675d6fb3e1188f2c5300a", "parents": ["f5f293bd79791b334f1aefb359231ce051eb73e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelsey Gilbert \u003ckelsey.gilbert@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1829756 - E.g. DeleteTexture in ~WebGLTextureJS. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman a=RyanVM\n\nOtherwise GCing will not release them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D176828", "files": ["dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0a9951339e8d78ab1e0a0db3a3e1174c2172de7b", "parents": ["5b4d602ef5a54aed21c675d6fb3e1188f2c5300a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Neil Deakin \u003cneil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1829981, reduce maximum filename length to 254, as Windows File Explorer won't allow deleting filenames longer than this, r=Gijs a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D176911", "files": ["uriloader/exthandler/nsExternalHelperAppService.cpp", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/save_filenames.html", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/unit/test_filename_sanitize.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d8b13fb73d8e1eafde1eff1764071dd20f6eb532", "parents": ["0a9951339e8d78ab1e0a0db3a3e1174c2172de7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1752703 - Move the pthread_thread_create() interposer under mozglue and prepare for having a single place where we place interposer functions r=glandium a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D164470", "files": ["browser/app/moz.build", "ipc/app/moz.build", "js/src/make-source-package.py", "js/xpconnect/shell/moz.build", "mozglue/interposers/InterposerHelper.h", "mozglue/interposers/moz.build", "mozglue/interposers/pthread_create_interposer.cpp", "mozglue/moz.build", "toolkit/crashreporter/moz.build", "toolkit/crashreporter/pthread_create_interposer/moz.build", "toolkit/crashreporter/pthread_create_interposer/pthread_create_interposer.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "24594061b59dd424d52aae6cccdebd264d29fa69", "parents": ["d8b13fb73d8e1eafde1eff1764071dd20f6eb532"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1752703 - Add interposers for functions manipulating the environment to prevent crashes r=glandium a=RyanVM\n\nThis add interposers for getenv(), putenv(), setenv(), unsetenv() and\nclearenv(). All interposers use a single lock for synchronization while\ninternally using the libc-provided functions. This is done to prevent races\nthat typically happen in Firefox code when multiple threads call getenv()\nwhile others are changing variables using setenv() and putenv().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D164471", "files": ["mozglue/interposers/env_interposer.cpp", "mozglue/interposers/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b9f1129e260717737c74082da2bf846758382219", "parents": ["24594061b59dd424d52aae6cccdebd264d29fa69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1827655, for consistency, make nsISHEntry implementations support weak references similarly to nsISHistory implementation, r=peterv a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178071", "files": ["docshell/shistory/SessionHistoryEntry.cpp", "docshell/shistory/SessionHistoryEntry.h", "docshell/shistory/nsSHEntry.cpp", "docshell/shistory/nsSHEntry.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5550c3f42b88afed72a0d7705cb711bacd25c295", "parents": ["b9f1129e260717737c74082da2bf846758382219"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1834066 - Update Search Engine URL for Gule sider. r=search-reviewers,daleharvey a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178800", "files": ["browser/components/search/extensions/gulesider-NO/manifest.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9a587b87adb244d36a7ef877094abb5dedffe228", "parents": ["5550c3f42b88afed72a0d7705cb711bacd25c295"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830795, part 1 - Convert gContentListHashTable to an nsTHashtable. r=nika a=RyanVM\n\nThis isn't necessary for the later parts, but I think it makes\nit easier to understand.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D177842", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentList.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "df550891a6ef1fa3cc66f75103f721fa85aa5789", "parents": ["9a587b87adb244d36a7ef877094abb5dedffe228"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830795, part 2 - Convert gFuncStringContentListHashTable to an nsTHashtable. r=nika a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D177843", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentList.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5dbc48703b7d0309118934f831fcb166dc28278e", "parents": ["df550891a6ef1fa3cc66f75103f721fa85aa5789"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830795, part 3 - Move content list cache entry classes into their list classes. r=nika a=RyanVM\n\nIn the next patch, I'm adding a field to nsContentList that I want these hash\ntable entries to be able to access, so I'm making them inner classes here.\n\nI've also renamed them to get rid of some redundancy, because\notherwise the qualified names would be long.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D177844", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentList.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentList.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "14fa844a994d57ba9f6767c5377eefda43bfac42", "parents": ["5dbc48703b7d0309118934f831fcb166dc28278e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830795, part 4 - Implement lifetime checking for content list cache entries. r=nika a=RyanVM\n\nAdd a new field to nsContentList that should be true if and only if\nthat list is in one of the hashtable caches.\n\nThe entry destructor release assert double checks that any list it contains\nknew it was in an entry. This should be superfluous as long as\nSetContentList is the only place that sets HashEntry::mContentList to a non-null\nvalue, and nsContentList::mInHashtable to true.\n\nThe first SetContentList release assert ensures that the entry starts out empty,\nbecause if it wasn't we'd need to tell the current list that it is being\nremoved from the cache entry.\n\nThe second SetContentList release assert ensures that the list is never in more\nthan one entry at the same time, which allows us to make mInHashtable a boolean\nand not an integer.\n\nThe release asserts in the remove-from-hashtable methods ensure that the list\nisn't in a hashtable afterwards. These are done as two separate checks to try to\nhelp with debugging if we see these asserts get hit. These methods are called\nfrom the destructor, and other places related to tearing down a content list.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178322", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentList.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentList.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "69a0927242a2241524d17d1be91323a2859129a3", "parents": ["14fa844a994d57ba9f6767c5377eefda43bfac42"], "tags": []}], "date": 1685043059, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "256": {"changesets": [{"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830206 - Add an arbitrary limit to the number of audio channels a media can have. r=alwu, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D177644", "files": ["dom/media/MediaInfo.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "838b4ee62cdf28ea26f21f6456869a73c12d6b11", "parents": ["69a0927242a2241524d17d1be91323a2859129a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830206 - Fix an overly restrictive assertion in the SPSC ringbuffer. r=alwu, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D177770", "files": ["mfbt/SPSCQueue.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1393c9aa14fb15f23d83ddb44bb3a6b4e3494cac", "parents": ["838b4ee62cdf28ea26f21f6456869a73c12d6b11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830206 - Rework AudioSink's ringbuffer size computation. r=alwu, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178074", "files": ["dom/media/mediasink/AudioSink.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3a6eed95ff5bbe3b3046d697f2f8b30fb45b361a", "parents": ["1393c9aa14fb15f23d83ddb44bb3a6b4e3494cac"], "tags": []}], "date": 1685111590, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "257": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr102 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update r=pascalc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D179348", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "436a2ee5bfc7c4e70c0d6bc14bf1946e66c1a231", "parents": ["3a6eed95ff5bbe3b3046d697f2f8b30fb45b361a"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_102_12_0esr_BUILD1", "FIREFOX_102_12_0esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1685380188, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}}
}";